<Layout title="What to Know Before Starting a Home Addition | ATECT Architecture" description="Key planning questions to consider before starting a home addition, from goals and existing conditions to budget, approvals, and construction documents.">
  <article class="article"><header><p class="eyebrow">Residential Planning</p><h1>What to Know Before Starting a Home Addition</h1><p class="lede">An addition affects more than the new square footage. Early decisions about goals, site conditions, budget, structure, and approvals can shape the entire project.</p></header>
  <section><h2>Start with the reason for the addition</h2><p>Define what the new space needs to accomplish. More bedrooms, a larger kitchen, a home office, improved circulation, and indoor-outdoor living can lead to very different design solutions.</p></section>
  <section><h2>Understand the existing house</h2><p>Existing dimensions, structure, roof geometry, utilities, openings, site conditions, and the relationship between old and new construction all influence what is possible.</p></section>
  <section><h2>Establish a realistic project framework</h2><p>Before design decisions become commitments, consider the desired scope, available budget, schedule, permitting path, and the level of documentation the project will require.</p></section>
  <section><h2>Design the addition as part of the whole</h2><p>A successful addition should address the new program while considering the proportions, materials, circulation, daylight, exterior character, and long-term function of the existing home.</p></section>
  <section class="callout"><h2>Planning an addition?</h2><p>ATECT Architecture can help evaluate the existing conditions, develop design options, and prepare the documentation needed to move the project forward.</p><a class="button dark" href="/contact">Start a Conversation</a></section>
  </article>
</Layout>
